WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.200
After almost twenty years, a new "Matrix"&nbsp;
movie is finally coming to theaters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.240
and set to blow us all away.&nbsp;
Who's back from the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:12.560
films and who's set to join the cast as&nbsp;
new faces? Are you beginning to believe?

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.440
When the news of a fourth "Matrix"&nbsp;
movie broke in Variety in August 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.080
producer and distributor Warner Bros.&nbsp;
didn't announce a release date for the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.640
It did say that production was scheduled&nbsp;
to begin sometime in early 2020.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:33.520
In December of 2019, Warner Bros. announced&nbsp;
a "Matrix 4" release date of May 21, 2021.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.560
Unlike "The Matrix" and "The Matrix Reloaded,"&nbsp;
which hit theaters in late March 1999&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:44.160
and mid-May 2003, respectively," the fourth&nbsp;
"Matrix" won't see a spring release, or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.920
an autumn one like "The Matrix Revolutions,"&nbsp;
which made its way to theaters in November 2003.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.720
Per The Hollywood Reporter, filming on "The&nbsp;
Matrix Resurrections" was paused in March 2020&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.440
over coronavirus spread concerns, and Warner&nbsp;
Bros, accounted for that delay by pushing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:05.440
scheduled release to April 2022. About six months&nbsp;
later, with production picking up, Warner moved up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.680
the release date to December 22, 2021. The same&nbsp;
day "The Matrix Resurrections" hits theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.560
it'll also be available to stream for&nbsp;
subscribers of HBO Max for a limited time.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.360
"I want it! Come on, gimme it.&nbsp;
Gimme it. Come on, give me it."

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.320
The special effects might have felt like the real&nbsp;
stars of "The Matrix" and its sequels, but those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:30.320
films wouldn't have been nearly as good or as&nbsp;
memorable if the human actors hadn't pulled their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.760
weight. Keanu Reeves proved his action hero turn&nbsp;
in "Speed" wasn't a fluke with his role as Neo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.640
Carrie-Anne Moss, at the time of the release of&nbsp;
"The Matrix" in 1999, was a little-known talent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.760
with a bunch of episodic television credits&nbsp;
to her name, but "The Matrix" made her a star.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:50.160
Reeves and Moss quickly locked in their&nbsp;
commitment to return to play Neo and Trinity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.040
One actor who definitely won't be back:&nbsp;
Hugo Weaving. Due to a scheduling conflict,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.440
he's not available to reprise his role as&nbsp;
the villainous Agent Smith. Lots of other big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:03.600
names played central roles in the "Matrix"&nbsp;
trilogy, like Laurence Fishburne and Jada&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:09.760
Pinkett-Smith. Fishburne won't reprise his role,&nbsp;
but Pinkett-Smith will, along with Lambert Wilson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.240
who played the Merovingian and Daniel&nbsp;
Bernhardt, who played Agent Johnson.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:20.240
In October 2019, the cast of "The Matrix&nbsp;
Resurrections" started to take shape. Neil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.800
Patrick Harris landed a role that the film's&nbsp;
trailer indicated was a therapist of some sort.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.440
Harris is primarily a TV performer, best&nbsp;
known for his work on "How I Met Your Mother"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:34.480
and "Doogie Howser, M.D.," and "The Matrix&nbsp;
Resurrections" will mark his biggest movie yet.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.360
Writer/director/producer Lana Wachowski saw&nbsp;
several actors for another secret part in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.080
"The Matrix Resurrections," later revealed to&nbsp;
be a character called Morpheus. The original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.880
Morpheus was made famous by Laurence Fishburne in&nbsp;
the original "Matrix" trilogy." The right man to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:54.640
possibly replace Fishburne for the job: Yahya&nbsp;
Abdul-Mateen II, a rising star thanks to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.760
scene-stealing performance in "The Get Down"&nbsp;
and his work in HBO's "Watchmen" miniseries.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:06.240
Another new member of the Matrix family: Priyanka&nbsp;
Chopra. According to Variety in January 2020, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.200
"Quantico" star underwent fight training for weeks&nbsp;
in anticipation of the film beginning production.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.760
In 2021, a Korean "Matrix Resurrection" poster&nbsp;
divulged that Chopra is playing the adult version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.600
of Sati, the child that the Oracle was taking&nbsp;
care of in 2003's "The Matrix Revolutions."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.760
Fans speculate that Sati may be the new&nbsp;
Oracle in "The Matrix Resurrections,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.120
but we still don't know for sure. Brian J. Smith&nbsp;
and Erendira Ibarra, best known for their work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.560
on the Wachowskis' Netflix series "Sense8,"&nbsp;
will also appear in "The Matrix Resurrections,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:43.360
as will Jessica Henwick, Christina&nbsp;
Ricci, Jonathan Groff, and Telma Hopkins.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Would it really be a "Matrix" movie if&nbsp;
Lana and Lily Wachowski weren't involved?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.960
After turning heads with the stylish 1996&nbsp;
crime drama "Bound," the Wachowskis made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.640
themselves legends with "The Matrix" in 1999,&nbsp;
unveiling a novel premise set in a marvelously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.840
realized universe. The siblings co-wrote and&nbsp;
co-directed "The Matrix," "The Matrix Reloaded,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.800
and "The Matrix Revolutions," but the reports&nbsp;
announcing "The Matrix Resurrections" don't note&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:14.080
the involvement of Lily Wachowski — Lana Wachowski&nbsp;
is evidently going solo this time around.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.600
Wachowski won't have to go it totally&nbsp;
alone, however — she'll direct from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.160
script co-written with literary figure&nbsp;
Aleksander Hemon and David Mitchell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.880
who both wrote an episode of the Wachowskis'&nbsp;
"Sense8" while Mitchell wrote "Cloud Atlas,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.680
turned into a film by the Wachowskis in&nbsp;
2012. John Toll, meanwhile, will handle the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.960
cinematography. He previously shot "Jupiter&nbsp;
Ascending" and "Cloud Atlas" for Wachowski,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.720
and won Academy Awards for his work on&nbsp;
"Legends of the Fall" and "Braveheart."

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:46.320
Prominently and suspiciously not mentioned&nbsp;
anywhere in Variety's August 2019 report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:49.760
about the launch of a then-untitled&nbsp;
fourth movie in "The Matrix" series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:55.040
was the key character known as Morpheus. Nobody&nbsp;
said anything about whether the mentor figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.880
would return for the new movie or not, nor&nbsp;
was there any mention of the involvement of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.800
Laurence Fishburne, the actor who played&nbsp;
the part in the original three movies.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.760
Not to worry, says Variety reporter Justin Kroll.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:09.600
Shortly after he published his story&nbsp;
about "The Matrix 4," he tweeted,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.480
"[S]ources have told me this may&nbsp;
point to where and when the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:17.040
is set as I've heard execs are looking a&nbsp;
variety of actors to possibly play [him]"

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.800
And that's about all we know about the plot.&nbsp;
The fact that Morpheus looks to be played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:26.400
by Yahya Abdul-Mateen II suggests "The Matrix&nbsp;
Resurrections" takes place in a different time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.480
than the original trilogy. Morpheus&nbsp;
was killed off in the Matrix: Online,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:35.680
an MMORPG that continued the story from the&nbsp;
original trilogy, but whether the game's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:40.640
events are still considered canon is unknown.&nbsp;
Perhaps Mateen II is playing a digital version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:46.240
of Morpheus based on a younger mind? Or is Mateen&nbsp;
II's character simply inspired by Morpheus?

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.320
"What do you think is happening right now?"

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:48.960
"It doesn't matter."

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.680
"It's good."

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.760
"We'll sort this out later,&nbsp;
it doesn't matter right now."

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.600
The news of the new "Matrix" movie with&nbsp;
most of the original cast and creators&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.280
means that a different "Matrix"-based&nbsp;
product is likely no longer happening.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:04.400
In March 2017, The Hollywood Reporter broke the&nbsp;
news that Warner Bros. had started preliminary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:09.760
development of a reboot/relaunch of "The Matrix."&nbsp;
Screenwriter Zak Penn, who wrote "X-Men: The Last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:15.040
Stand" and "Ready Player One," was reportedly in&nbsp;
talks to write a detailed narrative plot outline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.000
all because original "Matrix" producer Joel Silver&nbsp;
approached Warner Bros. with the suggestion of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:25.040
revival. The Wachowskis were not involved with&nbsp;
that project, and no actors signed up to star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.040
although initial reports hinted that Warner&nbsp;
Bros. would've liked to cast Michael B.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:33.360
Jordan. As Lana Wachowski, Keanu Reeves, and&nbsp;
Carrie-Anne Moss all reunited to make "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.720
Matrix Resurrections," this other new "Matrix"&nbsp;
is now old news. Perhaps that's for the best.

